# Live freeze-backdrop corpus - tests/harness/check_live_freeze_backdrop.sh
#
# Per row one headless capture and one windowed eager replay per tick scale,
# each to the frame limit; the live frozen_tex at the dump VBL is compared
# with the scene-only image of the last world present the leg displayed; the
# headless render of the canonical pin, extracted at the pin VBL, is the
# tick's own frame the displayed reference must differ from on some leg.
#
#   <bk2> | <frame-limit> | <dump VBL> | <pin VBL> | <launch tokens>
#
# `launch` takes the presentation-corpus convention: a whitespace-separated
# token spelled KEY=VALUE with an upper-case key is an environment entry,
# every other token a command-line argument. OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1
# puts the retained terrain cache under test on a software rasteriser;
# OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off bakes without a wall-time budget, so the
# live and headless legs bake the same sectors on the same ticks.
#
# pause-unpause: the pause starts at VBL 1669 after one gameplay tick, the
# scene extracted at VBL 1667; under eager presentation the presents before
# the pause are sub-tick re-extracts between the fade-in frame and it.
pause-unpause.bk2 | 1730 | 1700 | 1667 | --aspect 4:3 --no-card --lod original --render-paths terrain,spyro,ui OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off
